                    "prompt": "What is the shortest travelling time between $A$ and $E$?",
                    "answerSpaceMm": 32,
                    "answer": {
                      "short": "62 minutes.",
                      "worked": "Using Dijkstra’s algorithm from $A$, the lowest total times are $D=10$, $C=18$, then $B=\\min(50,10+32,18+28)=42$.\n\nFor $E$:\n$$\\begin{aligned}t_E&=\\min(10+80,18+50,42+20)\\\\&=\\min(90,68,62)\\\\&=62\\text{ minutes}.\\end{aligned}$$\nThe shortest route is $A-D-B-E$.",
